From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?John=20T=C3=B6rnblom?= <john.tornblom@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:14:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] egl: a videoout platform, zink on the PS4's display

-Dplatforms=videoout is EGL on the PlayStation 4's display (VideoOut),
through zink on RADV (-Dradv-winsys=ps4), which shows VideoOut with
VK_KHR_display. It is the console build's native platform
(-Degl-native-platform=videoout), and needs neither DRM nor a window
system; with it, gallium builds the DRI frontend for zink alone, as on
macOS.

- eglGetDisplay(EGL_DEFAULT_DISPLAY) opens zink through kopper, with no
  device node, on EGL's software device.
- The display is the only window: any non-zero EGLNativeWindowType names
  it, and window surfaces made from the same value share zink's
  swapchain. A window surface is the size of the display's mode
  (kopperQueryDisplayExtent), and kopper presents it to a display surface.
- Pbuffers are zink's own images, as on the surfaceless platform.
- Window configs are the formats VideoOut scans out, B8G8R8A8 and
  B8G8R8X8, linear or sRGB; every pbuffer visual is a pbuffer config.
- FIFO is the one present mode, so the swap interval is 0 or 1, and 0 is
  shown as 1. EGL_EXT_buffer_age and EGL_EXT_swap_buffers_with_damage are
  offered.

The build: the DRI frontend's dri2.c, which holds EGL's image and fence
entry points, is built for the platform as for macOS; System V shared
memory is used only where its calls exist, which the PS4's libc lacks; and
egl.pc and glesv2.pc hand the program RADV's system modules to link, as
vulkan.pc does, so that its crt initializes them.

A Linux build of the PS4 winsys's host model can build the platform too,
and runs the whole path, EGL to the VideoOut WSI's stand-ins, on a PC.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017iduBr5J43VcTC99HLCEQm
